{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Rebuke</b> — like הנני גוער לכם (behold, I rebuke you); it has no bet [as root letter]." "<b>Beast of</b> — as in חיתך ישבו בה (your beasts dwell in it)." "<b>Cane</b> — the beast whose spears are long, like the cane, and likewise the name for spears in the language of Kedar." "<b>Among the calves of the peoples</b> — like עדת אבירים (congregation of mighty ones); like אבירי בשן (mighty ones of Bashan), פרות הבשן (cows of Bashan); and the meaning is doubled." "<b>Rebuke</b> — them, until each one of them humbles himself before you." "<b>Bars of silver</b> — to give tribute. He said that all the people who wish to fight you will scatter." "<b>Scatter</b> — like ורכוש להם יבזור (and spoil for them he distributes)." "<b>And draw near</b> — like המלמד ידי לקרב (who trains my hands for battle)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 68, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:17.509567062Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}